WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:05.170
- [Interviewer] Okay, Floyd.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.063
So, tell me where you're from.

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:10.080
- My name is Floyd.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.660
I'm from Texas.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.210
- [Interviewer] And you've been out -

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.000
You came to Skid Row when?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.760
- [Floyd] I came to Skid
Row back in the mid '80s.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.776
- [Interviewer] Mid '80s?

00:00:19.776 --> 00:00:20.609
- Mm hmm.

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:21.800
- [Interviewer] You were selling.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.488
What drugs were you selling mostly?

00:00:23.488 --> 00:00:26.403
- I used to sell cocaine.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.810
I got turned on how to cook it.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.337
I know how to cut it.

00:00:33.337 --> 00:00:34.913
I know how to sell it.

00:00:35.813 --> 00:00:38.640
Because I was from the country, you know?

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.540
I want to make some fast money,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.593
that's what I did.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:44.923
- [Interviewer] Figure it out.

00:00:44.923 --> 00:00:46.940
- Yeah, figure it out, yeah.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.130
Older people schooling me

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.020
telling me how to do it,

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.900
how to sell it and stuff like that.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.040
- [Interviewer] And what sells?

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.240
What sold more?

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.373
The powder or the rock?

00:01:00.373 --> 00:01:03.190
- Well see, a lot of people

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:05.956
back then liked the rock.

00:01:05.956 --> 00:01:08.780
They really liked both,

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.840
but when you're selling both

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.920
you don't get much time for the powder

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.680
and then do the rock.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:20.215
You feel like the rock is

00:01:20.215 --> 00:01:23.440
the drug of people of color

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.170
and the powder is for
the mostly rich people

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.350
that snort powder.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.428
- [Interviewer] And your
customers would come from

00:01:31.428 --> 00:01:34.410
other parts of the city
as well as Skid Row?

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:37.213
- Yeah, they used to come from Hollywood,

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:43.870
Santa Monica, you know all over basically.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.710
All over, yes.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:46.740
- [Interviewer] You were
the place to get it.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:47.573
- Mm hmm, yes.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:48.470
- [Interviewer] How
much money did you make

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:50.060
typically in a day?

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.970
- Well, mostly the night time

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:58.570
I would make about maybe
$1500 or $1600 or more.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:01:59.403
- [Interviewer] At night?

00:01:59.403 --> 00:02:00.684
- Yeah, at night.

00:02:00.684 --> 00:02:01.517
- [Interviewer] That's good money.

00:02:01.517 --> 00:02:02.350
- Yes.

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:09.707
- [Interviewer] Were there
other dealers that were like

00:02:09.707 --> 00:02:11.390
"you're infringing on their territory?"

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:12.790
or vice versa?

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:15.930
- You know, we didn't really.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:19.350
No, back then we didn't have that problem

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.270
because being downtown is neutral.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.626
We don't have that problem.

00:02:22.626 --> 00:02:25.340
If I go to someone else's hood

00:02:26.552 --> 00:02:28.383
or other side of town

00:02:28.383 --> 00:02:32.300
I might have some infliction;

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.240
but downtown is really neutral.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.287
Downtown really neutral.

00:02:35.287 --> 00:02:36.770
- [Interviewer] And the cops,

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:41.149
did you ever get thrown
in jail for carrying it?

00:02:41.149 --> 00:02:44.470
- Yeah, I got thrown in jail.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:49.470
My first time going to
jail out here was in '86,

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:53.073
then I got out because
it was simply possession.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.203
But you know, back then

00:02:56.203 --> 00:03:00.900
they really didn't trip on
cocaine like they do now

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.320
because they didn't really
know too much about it.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.791
You know, another thing too

00:03:05.791 --> 00:03:10.340
it wasn't having a big effect on people

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.260
like it do to this day

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.330
because they put a whole bunch of cut

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.561
and a whole bunch of
different chemicals in there.

00:03:18.561 --> 00:03:22.190
Then you have some cocaine now it may be,

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.010
maybe I'm just exaggerating,

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:29.680
maybe 15 to 30 percent cocaine

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.540
the rest of it some garbage.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.210
'Cuz it only take just
a little cocaine base

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:40.430
for you to go to jail
or prison for you know,

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.620
and stuff like that.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.480
- [Interviewer] How many
years were you in prison?

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.510
- [Floyd] Okay, I went to prison.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.230
I went to prison.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.210
I got out for doing 7 years and 8 months.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:56.673
I got out January 1st, 2018.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.150
I went for a conspiracy case

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:04.420
because they said that
I sold to an undercover,

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:08.660
which they didn't have no
marked money or no dope on me.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:11.611
Only reason why they
convict me was my past.

00:04:11.611 --> 00:04:12.870
They convict me from my past.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.910
At first they said I sold to
an unidentified black male.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.030
That was the story at first,

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.400
then they said I sold to an undercover.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.360
They didn't cover no marked money

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.910
or no narcotic from me.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.020
- [Interviewer] How much time did you do?

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:31.172
- [Floyd] Okay, they gave me 17 years.

00:04:31.172 --> 00:04:33.572
With doing with good behavior,

00:04:33.572 --> 00:04:36.270
rehabilitating myself in prison,

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:41.270
I got on about 57 which I
did 7 years and 8 months.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:45.940
My release date was November 23rd, 2023

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:50.000
because I was 17 years and 80 percent,

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.413
you do 13 years and 4 months.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.830
Yes.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:55.680
- [Interviewer] Tell me
about your childhood.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:56.620
Did you -

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.818
Were drugs apart of your
childhood in any way?

00:04:58.818 --> 00:04:59.843
- [Floyd] You know, no.

00:05:00.762 --> 00:05:04.040
No, drugs never was a
part of my childhood.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.564
I really didn't know nothing about drugs

00:05:06.564 --> 00:05:09.210
'til I came to California.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.800
I was doing good in school.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.340
I was a good athlete, you know, in school.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:16.010
When I came out here I was a good athlete

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:18.680
but me being from the country

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:23.657
and making this type of
money was overwhelming.

00:05:23.657 --> 00:05:26.310
"I like this, I like that." You know?

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.320
And stuff like that.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:28.440
- [Interviewer] Did you
ever use it yourself?

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.570
- No, I never used.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:30.403
No, I never used.

00:05:30.403 --> 00:05:33.420
I never used no drugs
or anything like that.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:36.750
Only drug I tried is weed

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.310
and last time I smoked
some weed was in '94.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.081
- [Interviewer] All
right, you're not into it.

00:05:42.081 --> 00:05:43.596
- No, I'm not into it.

00:05:43.596 --> 00:05:45.560
No.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:47.130
- [Interviewer] Can you
tell me about the lifestyle?

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.453
What hours would you keep
when you were selling?

00:05:49.453 --> 00:05:51.449
- Well, when I was in school

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:56.449
I tried to hurry and finish
my basketball practice stuff

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.400
so I could come out and sell

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.100
till at least till about 10 o'clock

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:04.850
because I gotta be in the
house and go to school

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:06.229
the next morning.

00:06:06.229 --> 00:06:07.493
- [Interviewer] 10? 10 AM?

00:06:07.493 --> 00:06:09.329
- Nah, 10 at night.

00:06:09.329 --> 00:06:11.700
I go to school right,

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.720
then I got to school I got practice

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.320
until about 4 and 5, maybe 6.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:21.930
Then when I get,

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:24.851
I be trying to hurry up
and get through practice

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:26.340
so I can get out and make some money

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.910
before 10 o'clock at night

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.891
cause that's when my curfew was.

00:06:29.891 --> 00:06:30.991
- [Interviewer] Oh I see.

00:06:30.991 --> 00:06:32.373
- Yeah, that's what my curfew was.

00:06:32.373 --> 00:06:33.300
- [Interviewer] Some of the guys

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.762
were selling through the night.

00:06:34.762 --> 00:06:35.595
- Yes, through the night.

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:36.940
- [Interviewer] Did you ever do that?

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.199
- On weekends I did.

00:06:38.199 --> 00:06:40.193
On weekends, yes.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:49.150
- [Interviewer] So your
customers would just know

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:51.780
what corner you stood on
or where you hung out?

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:55.730
- Yes, you know, they did.

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:58.930
When you build your clientele up,

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.380
people gonna look for you.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.608
People ain't gonna go to no where else

00:07:02.608 --> 00:07:04.130
because they know they
ain't going to get beat,

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:05.690
they know they ain't going to get robbed,

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.397
they gonna get treated fairly.

00:07:07.397 --> 00:07:09.000
When I used to sell,

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.140
I used to treat my customers fairly.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:14.070
I used to treat them fairly.

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:15.060
- [Interviewer] Yeah, they
could always count on you.

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:16.540
- Yeah, they always could count on me.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:17.373
Yes.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:20.710
- [Interviewer] And, a
lot of addicts down here

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:21.690
on Skid Row so,

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:24.280
you had these people right
here in the neighborhood.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.366
- Yeah, you know.

00:07:25.366 --> 00:07:29.156
Since I been out, you know,
people still approach me

00:07:29.156 --> 00:07:32.290
or ask me "Do you got
anything? Do you got anything?"

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:34.110
Nope. I'm working.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:35.710
I got my life together.

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:38.438
I'm not doing that no more.

00:07:38.438 --> 00:07:39.439
- [Interviewer] That's good for you.

00:07:39.439 --> 00:07:41.422
- Yeah.

00:07:41.422 --> 00:07:42.910
- [Interviewer] You'll
stay out of jail that way.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:43.743
- Yes, yes.

00:07:43.743 --> 00:07:44.576
Yes sir.

00:07:47.465 --> 00:07:51.040
- [Interviewer] So your wife passed away?

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:56.040
- Yes, so she passed away in
2010 while I was in prison.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:58.063
- [Interviewer] Oh wow.

00:07:58.063 --> 00:07:58.896
- Yeah, while I was in prison.

00:07:58.896 --> 00:07:59.975
- [Interviewer] Any your kids?

00:07:59.975 --> 00:08:01.380
- No we don't have no kids.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.213
- [Interviewer] So you're on your own now?

00:08:02.213 --> 00:08:03.070
- Yeah, I'm on my own now.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:04.520
Yes.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.110
- [Interviewer] So Floyd,
what's the craziest thing

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:06.943
you remember -

00:08:06.943 --> 00:08:07.780
like when you were selling?

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:09.380
What kind of -

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.290
I'm sure you had stories

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.810
when you were out in
the streets doing this.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:17.080
- Yeah, the craziest thing you see

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:21.711
that how females know the greatest stuff

00:08:21.711 --> 00:08:24.250
about the product and stuff.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:27.730
You know, they do
anything for that product

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.363
when they don't have no money.

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:33.447
You know, I look back at it now

00:08:33.447 --> 00:08:37.910
and I really feel bad
to how I took advantage

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.740
of vulnerable people in that situation

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.690
when they feigning and stuff like that.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:44.440
To be honest with you,

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.950
I asked the lord to forgive me

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:49.240
for all the people that I hurt

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:51.303
that I sold that stuff to.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:54.823
On my conscious, it's clear.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.635
I'm through that lifestyle.

00:08:59.635 --> 00:09:00.960
I'm through with it.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.995
It took me a while to
wake up and learn that

00:09:04.995 --> 00:09:06.093
but I'm done with it.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.673
And if people out there doing it,

00:09:09.673 --> 00:09:12.580
there's more better ways

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:14.853
then life that hustle.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.580
Show money, slow money,

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:19.413
is sure money.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:23.310
You don't gotta worry about
living over your shoulder

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:24.578
when you got a 9 to 5.

00:09:24.578 --> 00:09:25.411
(laughs)

00:09:25.411 --> 00:09:27.129
You don't, you really don't.

00:09:27.129 --> 00:09:28.420
You really don't.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.673
- [Interviewer] Where do
you see yourself in 5 years?

00:09:31.648 --> 00:09:35.093
- Well, I see myself in 5 years,

00:09:36.247 --> 00:09:38.630
I'm going to intend to work

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:43.661
and I'd like to be a counselor.

00:09:43.661 --> 00:09:45.740
I got certificates

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.380
and I feel to be a counselor

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:48.700
help people out

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:53.600
and don't make the same
mistakes I made in my past

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:58.600
because selling drugs is
not no future in that.

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:03.360
It took me a later age to realize that.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.340
Now I woke up before it's too late.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:09.700
I'm still blessed with my health

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.423
and doing stuff like that.

00:10:13.466 --> 00:10:15.940
Five years I'd like to help people.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:17.290
I'd like to be a counselor.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:20.848
- [Interviewer] All right well,

00:10:20.848 --> 00:10:21.856
thank you for talking to me.

00:10:21.856 --> 00:10:22.778
- You welcome sir.

00:10:22.778 --> 00:10:23.611
- [Interviewer] All right.

00:10:23.611 --> 00:10:24.444
- All right then.

00:10:24.444 --> 00:10:25.277
- [Interviewer] Be safe out there.

00:10:25.277 --> 00:10:26.610
- Thank you sir.

